Test that the echo controller is made anew only when recording starts again

WebRTC's audio state with its patch 0009, a mock audio device that keeps whether it
records and a mock audio processing: the echo controller is made anew once each time
recording starts (a call, the microphone on again with nothing else sending, the next
call starting with recording), never while a shared screen's sound or another
connection's voice comes and goes, nor when recording fails to start. Built in again
with the mocks: the library shows only its own API.

